<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sandalj Hranić Kosača</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1370–<a href="/years/1435">1435</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Sandalj Hranić</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sandalj Hranić Kosača was a Bosnian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> who held the title of Grand Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and ruled Hum and the Adriatic hinterland as a nearly independent lord. He played kings of Bosnia, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> against one another and had close but difficult dealings with Ragusa, to which he sold part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/konavle">Konavle</a> in 1419. His nephew Stjepan Vukčić inherited his lands in 1435.</p></div>
